1 0 0 1 62.69291 550.8661 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (Key length mainly affects the cost of individual string comparisons, whereas insertion order has a) Tj T* (direct effect on BST height. A balanced BST provides O\(log n\) search in the usual balanced case,) Tj T* (while an ordinary skewed BST can degrade to O\(n\), which is the same asymptotic worst case as) Tj T* (linear search.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 62.69291 499.8661 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 34.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (Therefore, as the identification database grows, a self-balancing BST such as an AVL tree or) Tj T* (Red-Black tree is a suitable approach for maintaining efficient searches. For very large persistent) Tj T* (databases, B-tree / B+ tree based indexing is also commonly suitable.) Tj T* ET
Q
